es: Goomba tiles at $B0-$B3? Let me not rely on memory; the task says search PRG for the Goomba's tile ids in the order the game draws them.\n\nSo first step: determine the Goomba's tile IDs from the running game (list_sprites on the Goomba) and/or the mapping. Then search PRG for that byte sequence.\n\nPlan:\n1. Load persist-edit skill.\n2. Look at screen.\n3. Get to 1-1 gameplay: press Start, wait, press Start.\n4. Play right until Goomba near, pause, list_sprites to find Goomba's tiles.\n5. search_memory prgRom for the pattern.\n6. Check the hit by reading the table region and understanding.\n7. new_hack, use_hack.\n8. write_memory prgRom one byte (ledgered), reset, start 1-1, screenshot showing Goomba with different tile.\n9. undo_edit, clear.\n10. record_mapping note with rom_origins.\n11. promote_mappings, use_hack default.\n\nLet's start. Load skill and take initial screenshots in parallel.\n\nNote \"Mapping sheet 2 (where the pictures come from)\" — probably one of a set of mapping sheets; the game's mapping may already include Goomba tiles recorded. read_nametable includes tile names if a game mapping is loaded; but the Goomba is a sprite, not nametable. Perhaps the mapping file includes sprite mappings. Maybe I can find via record_mapping? There's no \"get mappings\" tool. Hmm, maybe lookup_symbol would answer from mapping? No, that's for references.\n\nMaybe the existing mapping is echoed in the system context normally (Current ROM section) but here it's not shown. Let's just do the work.\n\nLet me start."}
