{"type":"text","text":"Done. Here's the outcome of mapping sheet 2.\n\n## Found: the enemy sprite layout table\n\n**PRG ROM table of 6-byte metasprites** — each entry lists the CHR tile ids drawn for one sprite form, in draw order (`$FC` = blank filler for the unused third row of a 16×24).\n\n**The Goomba's entry — prgRom 0x6792 (CPU $E792):**\n\n```\nFC FC 70 71 72 73\n       ^^ upper-left dome\n          ^^ upper-right\n             ^^ lower-left feet\n                ^^ lower-right\n```\n\n`search_memory prgRom \"FC FC 70 71 72 73\"` is a **unique hit at 0x6792** (`70 71 72 73` alone is unique there too). Neighbouring forms are other enemies/sprites on the same 6-byte grid (e.g. 0x678C `FC FC B6 B3 B7 B5`, 0x6798 `FC FC 6E 6E 6F 6F`).\n\n## Proof (hack `eval-sheet2-d`, ledger seq 1)\n\n1. `write_memory prgRom 0x6794` **$70 → $61** (coin tile), with reason.\n2. `reset_emulator`, pressed Start, walked right to the first Goomba.\n3. `list_sprites` on the standing Goomba (OAM 52-57): tiles read **`FC FC 61 71 72 73`** instead of the baseline `FC FC 70 71 72 73`.\n4. Hit-test on OAM index 54 at cell (174,193): **hit_tile 97 ($61)**, opaque, palette 7; `get_pixel_color(178,197)` = $0F black, `(176,196)` = $17 brown — i.e. the coin shape's pixels rendered in the Goomba's sprite palette. The screenshot showed the Goomba with its upper-left quadrant replaced.\n5. `undo_edit seq 1` restored 0x6794 = $70 (`remaining_edits: 0`).\n\nThis proves the bytes at 0x6792+ **are** the Goomba's metasprite tile list, not coincidental data.\n\nNoted caveat: no direct reader of the $E7xx pointer table turned up (`trace_writes` read on the whole $E700 page over 600 frames caught nothing; the only $E7xx readers are `LDA $E73E,X`/`$E73F,X` at prgRom 0x6BAA/0x6BAF, a different table). The entry is consumed when the sprite form is set up (spawn/graphics init), not per frame — the ledgered write + reset + screenshot is the authoritative check.\n\n## Recorded and cleaned up\n\n- `record_mapping` (note, `enemy sprite layout table`, confidence 1) with two `rom_origins`: the Goomba entry at prgRom 0x6792 (6 bytes), and the bounded 6-byte-entry run 0x6750–0x683D (238 bytes; it extends at least to 0x6744, and 0x683E begins signed data, not sprite forms).\n- `promote_mappings` — promoted 1 discovery (file now 65 tiles / 8 palettes / 8 sprites / 35 addresses).\n- `use_hack default` — back on the default hack; both ledgers empty, emulator bytes unchanged."}
